<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Intercatia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Intercatia was a town of the Vaccaei in the northern Meseta of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, in the region of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zamora">Zamora</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valladolid">Valladolid</a>. In 151 BCE it was besieged by the Roman consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-licinius-lucullus">Lucius Licinius Lucullus</a>, and according to ancient writers the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-aemilianus">Scipio Aemilianus</a> won a single combat there against a Vaccaean champion. The town eventually surrendered on terms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/intercatia.jpg" alt="Intercatia" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jordi Malanyeu · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ermita_del_Cristo_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
